# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Generated by `npm run test:coverage`. Tracking it meant every coverage run
# dirtied ~33 files of regenerated HTML, which buried real diffs in review.
coverage

# Generated by `npm run test:mutation` (Stryker) — same reasoning as coverage:
# a regenerated HTML report is not a reviewable diff. `.stryker-tmp` is the
# sandbox Stryker copies the project into (tempDirName in stryker.conf.json).
# It must NOT live under node_modules: vite skips tsconfig for files under
# node_modules, so `useDefineForClassFields` is lost in the sandbox, model
# class fields serialise in a different key order and the payload golden
# tests fail the Stryker dry run.
reports
.stryker-tmp

